# `node_modules/` with a trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY only. In a round
# worktree `scripts/round-setup.sh` links it, and a SYMLINK named node_modules
# is not a directory — so `git add -A` staged it, with an absolute machine path
# as its blob content, and only `tests/privacy.spec.js` caught it. Match both.
node_modules
node_modules/
dist/
dev-dist/
*.local
.DS_Store
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Kid data and private material — never commit these.
deploy/sync-data/
compounded-backup-*.json
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
deploy/.env
!deploy/.env.example

# generated colouring-book output (regenerate with scripts/coloringbook.mjs).
# Reference photographs and scratch tooling stay out; the JUDGE'S EVIDENCE does
# not. docs/COIN-JUDGE.md 1.1 promises any number ever published can be
# reproduced and a retired instrument kept at its old hash — unkeepable if the
# scorecards, derivations and eval libraries only ever live on one disk.
# Text and instruments are tracked (~0.4 MB); the 15 MB of PNGs are not.
coloringbook/*
# THE EVAL LIBRARIES THE JUDGE'S GATES IMPORT (ledger A22/A25). These eight
# modules are not "scratch tooling": they are the code the PRIMARY GATE runs,
# and `coloringbook/*` above kept them out of the repository, so 63 of 286
# instruments — including T1 — could not run in any worktree or fresh clone and
# §1.1's reproducibility promise did not hold for them. Their SHA-256s are
# already quoted in _jd0hashes.json, _jp0hashes.json, penny-scorecard.json,
# nickel-scorecard.json and quarter-scorecard.json; the bytes tracked here are
# those exact bytes, so nothing a round published moves by tracking them.
# 638 lines, 52 KB. Anything ADDED here must be code an instrument imports.
!coloringbook/_nkdisc.mjs
!coloringbook/_pyellipse.mjs
!coloringbook/_pyseg.mjs
!coloringbook/_qtdisc.mjs
!coloringbook/_qtedge.mjs
!coloringbook/_qtseg.mjs

# FROZEN ARTEFACTS OF RECORD (ledger A46). Same argument as the eight modules
# above, one level down: these five are HASHED INTO THE FROZEN MANIFEST, so
# their bytes are cited — and `coloringbook/*` kept them out of the repository,
# meaning the hashes could not be checked anywhere but this disk. An instrument
# that cannot run is obvious the moment someone runs it; an artefact of record
# that cannot be checked is not. They carry no absolute path and no
# machine-local value (verified before tracking, and tests/privacy.spec.js runs
# over tracked files, so it now guards them too). 42 KB.
# Anything ADDED here must be an artefact some published number depends on.
!coloringbook/_nkparts.json
!coloringbook/_nkreg5.json
!coloringbook/_p2fam.json
!coloringbook/_pyout.json
!coloringbook/_x6-run.json
!coloringbook/_rvdisc.mjs
!coloringbook/_rvnorm.mjs
!coloringbook/judge/
coloringbook/judge/*
!coloringbook/judge/*.md
!coloringbook/judge/*.json
!coloringbook/judge/*.jsonl
!coloringbook/judge/*.mjs
# Retirement is by MOVE, never delete (COIN-JUDGE.md 1.1), so judge/retired/
# holds the old hash of every instrument that ever published a number. It is
# evidence for the same reason judge/ itself is, and needs its own un-ignore
# rules because the `coloringbook/judge/*` line above re-ignores the subtree.
!coloringbook/judge/retired/
coloringbook/judge/retired/*
!coloringbook/judge/retired/*.md
!coloringbook/judge/retired/*.json
!coloringbook/judge/retired/*.jsonl
!coloringbook/judge/retired/*.mjs
# NO TRACED DERIVATIVE IS COMMITTED. A carve-out here previously tracked
# `_jd2target-*.png` — a silhouette TRACED from three third-party cameo proof
# photographs — in a PUBLIC repository, while PROVENANCE-dime-proofs.md promises
# those references are "never redistributed, never traced". That contradiction
# was written by the judge and caught by the image review. Reverted.
# Reproducibility does not require it: `_jd2freeze.mjs` regenerates the target
# deterministically (verified byte-identical across two independent runs) and
# `_jd2target-dime-reverse.json` — which IS tracked — carries its SHA-256. The
# generator plus the hash is the evidence; the derivative image is not.

# Machine-specific values for judge instruments (host names, LAN addresses,
# scratch dirs). Read via coloringbook/judge/_paths.mjs `local()`. The example
# is tracked; the real file never is — this is what stopped a username from
# being committed into a public repo on 2026-08-23.
judge.local.json

# Agent worktrees (isolated checkouts; never part of a commit)
.claude/worktrees/
